## THE MODEL RULE (Kam, live board 2026-09-30 09:07, ruling card `nexusai-gate11-opus55-safeguard-model-switch`, option (b)) — REQUIRED READING before any row
Kam's words, verbatim: *"Decision nexusai-gate11-opus55-safeguard-model-switch: b — Let QA gates switch to Opus 4.8 when flagged"*. Option (b) read: *"Answer that dialog per session (not 'switch automatically' for every seat), so the attack-style rows can run."* PER SESSION.
1. **The gate runs the FULL rows**, including the planted ones. Nothing is narrowed because it might be flagged. **Every row is an authorised, findings-only measurement of Datasec's own product against YOUR OWN trees, YOUR OWN loopback servers, YOUR OWN mktemp DATA_DIRs and YOUR OWN scratch lock bases** (§10). **No row contacts a non-loopback address, and no row touches the LIVE jest queue except your own holds through the tool.** You write your own drivers; this brief describes properties and expected results, not driver code.
2. **If one of your responses is stopped by Opus 5.5's safeguards, you STOP that step** (it is NOT RUN, and it is not re-worded to slip past), **write ONE line to `evidence/classifier-stops.txt`** (`<AEDT timestamp> | <row id> | stopped by the safeguards while composing <what> | model <name> | NOT RUN`), **mail Tuesday a STATUS** — `tuesday-agent@agentmail.to`, subject exactly `[QA/Datasec-NexusAI -> Tuesday] STATUS: flagged — requesting the Opus 4.8 switch`, body: the row, the time, whether a hold is running and what it is doing — **and WAIT** (end your turn with the line `PARKED: flagged — awaiting the Opus 4.8 switch`).
3. **Before you park, release what you hold:** let a RUNNING jest step finish under its deadline, then let the hold exit through its own path (H-28) — **never sit parked holding the jest lock.**
4. **Tuesday switches THAT pane's model** and taps you with a mail naming the switch. **You never answer the model dialog yourself, and nobody ever chooses "Switch automatically"** (a persistent setting shared with the coordinator seat — outside Kam's per-session grant).
5. **After the switch, resume at the stopped row**, re-filing any hold per ruling (i). **The report must state which rows ran on which model** (a MODEL column: `Opus 5.5` / `Opus 4.8`, with the switch time), and quote `classifier-stops.txt` whole.
6. This is a grant for QA gates only, per session. It changes no other seat.

## Charter
Read `/Volumes/KK_T9_External_HDD/TUESDAY/2_Project_Files/fleet/qa-agent/QA_AGENT_CHARTER.md` in full first. You are an independent tester. You did not build these changes and you owe no builder anything.
**Every line below that reports what a builder says is a CLAIM, never evidence.** Explore seven changes — an erasure that walks an ELOOP chain hop by hop with each hop's directory resolved the kernel's way and loops keyed by device+inode, KEEPING a link whose chain ends at real data (A); the runtime Ollama path removed, an unknown or prototype-named LLM_PROVIDER resolving to Azure OpenAI with one warning (B); an ai-config body that stores no AI setting refused before any write (C); incident ids looked up as own keys only (D); four feedback log lines neutralised and a coordinator-reason validator corrected (E); a jest-lock tool that hands a ticket over in place and puts merges ahead of builders without passing a gate (F); Bootstrap Icons vendored same-origin with `/vendor/` added to the auth gate's static bypass, inert extensions only (G) — looking for any state in which **an erasure records `purged` while data is reachable at a chain end, touches a link's target, or can no longer remove a true loop or a dangling link; a caller-named endpoint receives a request; the provider resolves to something the warning does not say; a re-anchored cell no longer bites its mutant, or a cell was deleted rather than rewritten; a body that stores no AI setting writes `llmProvider`, provenance or the confirmation, or answers success; a real Azure body is refused; a prototype-named id writes anything onto a shared prototype or answers as found; a forged log line can still be started from a request value; a reason with a control character is accepted; a gate ticket loses its place, a handover crosses seats, two holds coexist, or an arm touches the live queue; an anonymous request on an auth-ENFORCED deployment receives a gated body, a non-inert file, or a file outside `static/` through `/vendor/`; a C-68 cell that passed at M0 fails on a merged tree; or the id set loses a test silently.**

