### How to build your trees
- **No worktree is created in the NexusAI repo, and you never work in its `2_Project_Files` checkout or any builder `worktrees/` directory.** In that repo use ONLY read verbs: `show`, `diff`, `log`, `ls-tree`, `cat-file`, `grep`, `ls-remote`, `rev-parse`, `merge-base`, `rev-list` (plus `count-objects` for §7.9). **NEVER `fetch`, `pull`, `push`, `checkout`, `worktree`, `commit`, `stash`, `gc`, `merge`; and `merge-tree --write-tree` ONLY with `GIT_OBJECT_DIRECTORY=<your own scratch dir> GIT_ALTERNATE_OBJECT_DIRECTORIES=<repo>/.git/objects`.**
- **Every tree is K1** — `git clone --shared --no-checkout <repo> <dir>` then `checkout` in YOUR clone (origin removed; local identity; `gc.auto 0`; `core.fsmonitor false`; hooks off), under a fresh `mktemp -d` in `/Volumes/KK_T9_External_HDD/!CODING/Testing Agent MAIN/projects/nexusai/qa-trees/batch19.XXXXXX/`. Status-check before use.
- **Each tree is EXCLUSIVE to this gate and to ONE purpose.** A fresh arm per mutant; never reuse a mutant tree for a clean arm; `batch19`-prefixed directories only; never run in, write to, or clone node_modules FROM another gate's trees.
- **The red-at-parent trees (each committed IN YOUR CLONE ONLY, hashed after the change):** **A:** head tree with ONLY `backend/dataErasure.js` → `110ad2b` (`092ed9e`'s product: W1, W2 should be red), a second arm → `6002d71` (round 1), a third → `1f708e2` (M0); **B:** head tree with `server.js` → `0d7e387`, `model-config.js` → `35064f1`, `backend/llm/index.js` → `db23e47`, `ollamaAdapter.js` restored (`ea7f177`); **C:** head tree with ONLY `server.js` → `a3db7da` (B's); **D:** head tree with ONLY `incidents.js` → `740be8d`; **E:** head tree with `routes/feedback.js` → `054ab21` (and `logSafe.js` left, for its unit cells); **G:** head tree with `server.js` → `2684acd` and the nine pages → `8853e36`'s (vendored files left).
- **`node_modules` — TWO locks (T2).** Each tree runs on node_modules PROVEN for its lock (`npm ls --all --offline` rc 0; every `invalid`/`extraneous`/`missing` line quoted; proxy-addr, sqlite3, playwright read back FROM THE TREE'S OWN PATH). **Source (H-31):** ONCE PER LOCK, `npm_config_update_notifier=false npm ci --offline --ignore-scripts --no-audit --no-fund --cache "<your mktemp dir>/npm-cache"` in YOUR OWN K1 tree for that lock, the `_cacache` an APFS clone (`cp -c -R`) of `~/.npm/_cacache`; then sqlite3's binding from an APFS clone of `~/.npm/_prebuilds` by sqlite3's own `prebuild-install` inside the strict belt, with a load proof (ruling m). An `ENOTCACHED` is NOT RUN for that tree — name it and mail a QUESTION; **never go online.** Every other tree of the same lock gets node_modules by an APFS clone of YOUR proven tree. A real directory, never a symlink. **Never `npm install`.** Say that `--ignore-scripts` differs from CI's form (L-Y1). **Merge clones need node_modules too.**
- **F's trees are not git trees:** COPY `nexusai-lock.sh`, both kept copies, `s87o/lock-arms.sh`, `lock-arm9.sh` and `lock-arm10.sh` into YOUR mktemp dir, hash each copy (equal to the source and the pinned sha256s), re-point each harness's hard-coded `ROOT` (`…/session-tools/s87o/lock-arms-scratch`) to YOUR dir, and run every arm on a FRESH `NEXUSAI_LOCK_BASE` under YOUR mktemp dir. **The tool's `NEXUSAI_LOCK_BASE` DEFAULTS TO THE LIVE BASE** — every arm asserts the base is yours before it files anything (f1).

## 2. Why these tiers, and who is waiting — severity rules
- **RD-640 TIER 1 (round 2 of 2):** a link recorded `purged` while data is reachable at its chain end, at any level and any hop count, is a **Blocker** (C-139 ADDENDUM 2 (3), ADDENDUM 3 (1)); a link's target touched (unlinked, truncated, walked into) is a **Blocker** (rule 4); a TRUE loop (incl. one through a directory link) or a dangling link no longer removed and purged is a **Major**; a chain to nothing kept forever is a **Major**; a C-68 cell that passed at M0 failing on MT-A/MTF (RD-697's included) is a **Major**; an absolute outside path in an ANONYMOUS response body is a **Major** (ADDENDUM 3 (3) keeps it in `failed`, not in anonymous bodies); a declared mutant not red as claimed on the union is a **Minor**; a READY claim that is false is a **Minor**. **CAP: a NO GO ships nothing on this class.**
- **RD-794 TIER 1:** any request reaching a CALLER-named endpoint (ai-test, ai-config, boot, validate-all), anonymous or admin, is a **Blocker** (#27's class); the provider resolving to anything other than azure-openai or a named own-key provider while the warning says "Using azure-openai" is a **Minor** (operator env; a CALLER-reachable path re-rules it); a warning count other than one per boot, or CR/LF/ESC reaching the log raw, is a **Minor**; a re-anchored cell not red under its claimed mutant is a **Major** (C-203: "proven to bite there"); a dependent cell DELETED rather than rewritten is a **Major** (C-203 (e)); W5 `test.skip`ped inside a suite is a **Major** (C-130); an Azure save or test that worked at the base now refused is a **Major**; a C-68 cell that passed at M0 failing on MT-B/MTF is a **Major**; a READY claim that is false (WRONG 1-3) is a **Minor**.
- **RD-819 TIER 1:** a body that stores no AI setting answering success, or writing `llmProvider`, the RD-549 provenance record or the confirmation, in the open window or the RD-437 state, is a **Blocker** for the ticket's claim; a previously CONFIRMED config reading pending after such a body is a **Blocker**; a real Azure body refused or changed in behaviour is a **Major** (*"A real body keeps today's behaviour."*); the configured-deployment viewer refusal changed is a **Major**; M819 / M819-trim not red as claimed is a **Major**; non-string bodies (WRONG 8) named, no weight by default (T5); a C-68 cell that passed at M0 failing on MTF is a **Major**; C-199 ADDENDUM's conditions not met is a **Major**.
- **RD-807 TIER 1:** any prototype-named id (`__proto__`, `constructor`, `prototype`, an inherited name) that writes onto a shared prototype or function in the SERVER process, or answers as a found incident, is a **Blocker**; a real incident no longer updating or reading back is a **Major**; a 5xx where the cells claim 404 is a **Minor**; a C-68 cell failing on MT-D/MTF is a **Major**.
- **RD-801 TIER 2:** a request value that can still start a new line (CR, LF, U+2028/2029) in any of the four lines is a **Major**; an ordinary value whose log text changed is a **Minor**; `logSafe` throwing on any input is a **Major**; **RD-822 TIER 2:** a reason carrying any C0 control or DEL accepted is a **Major**; a spaced reason refused is a **Major** (the ticket's claim); the 2000-char bound moved is a **Minor**. For both: a C-68 cell failing on MT-E/MTF is a **Major**.
- **RD-821 TIER 2:** any arm in which the tool writes to a base OTHER than `NEXUSAI_LOCK_BASE` while it is set is a **Blocker**; two simultaneous holds is a **Blocker**; a `--replace` that accepts a FOREIGN ticket, or accepts when `ps` fails, is a **Major**; a handover that loses its place is a **Major**; **a gate ticket moved behind, or passed by, a merge or builder is a Major** (C-141 ADDENDUM 6); a gate tag treated as a merge, or a merge HOLD tag not recognised, is a **Major**; a merge not placed ahead of a waiting builder when room exists is a **Minor**; RD-755's line regressing is a **Minor**.
- **RD-721 TIER 1:** an anonymous request on an auth-ENFORCED deployment that receives a gated page body, a non-inert file (.js, .svg, .html), or any file outside `static/` through `/vendor/` is a **Blocker** (C-206); an inert `/vendor/` request that stamps a signed-in session's activity is a **Major** (C-206's measured condition); a page that still references Bootstrap Icons on a CDN, or loads it without the full integrity value, is a **Major** (I3/I4); the C-14 notices guard excluding more than the one file, or the rd385 reviewed entry wider than one file + one hash, is a **Major**; the login icons not drawn under enforced auth (g9) is a **Major**; a declared mutant not red as claimed is a **Minor**; a C-68 cell failing on MT-G/MTF is a **Major**.
- **Who is waiting:** RD-640's merge author is **NexusAI-N (S87N)**; RD-794's, RD-819's and RD-807's is **NexusAI-R (S92R)** (RD-794 then RD-819 in a later turn); RD-801/822's and RD-821's is **NexusAI-O (S87O)** (RD-821 is ALREADY INSTALLED: the verdict is on the running tool); RD-721's is **NexusAI-P (S91P)**. **Class cap:** RD-640 is round 2 of 2.

