## 9. Floor discipline — THE FOUR CLAUSES, plus MERGES GO FIRST and THE DEADLINE RULE
1. **MERGES GO FIRST (ruling i).** **The jest lock `session-tools/nexusai-lock.sh` (queue `session-tools/locks/queue-jest/`) is shared with the builder seats** (at 14:3x AEDT the lock was HELD by `s92r-rd761-fix-proof` and `s87o-rd802-hold` was waiting — READ).
   - **Do ALL lock-free work first:** pins, reads, merge-trees in scratch objects, the offline `npm ci` (H-31), the plain-node, server, browser and lock-arm rows, census greps, prior-work reads, CI reads.
   - **Then file your holds (H-28), ONE AT A TIME**, each tagged `qa-b19-…` (e.g. `qa-b19-H1`), each a tracked child of your seat. **If a MERGE ticket is queued AHEAD of you, you wait behind it (that is FIFO). If a MERGE ticket files BEFORE YOUR GRANT, re-file behind it** (stop YOUR OWN unstarted waiter by pid from your own ancestry — C-174, never by pattern — confirm `released/` shows `ticket-left-*`, re-queue with `--after <that merge tag>` under your UNCHANGED tag). **At a wait deadline: `--replace` (ruling i).** Record each re-file with its place before and after FROM THE QUEUE LISTING. **Once your hold is GRANTED, carry on** — a running hold is never interrupted.
   - C-141: your hold is gate-class; builder PROOF tickets self-apply ONE yield per gate TAG. **QUEUE, NEVER TAKE OVER:** never kill, signal, move or edit another seat's process, lock directory, owner file or ticket, even if it looks stuck; if a holder looks stuck, mail a QUESTION (§11) and keep waiting.
2. **Hold the lock for a planned block of work, never idle (H-28)** — at most ~40 minutes of planned jest per hold, one hold at a time. Every hold is a TRACKED CHILD of your seat, never detached (`nohup … &`).
3. **Count foreign servers the C-125 way, anchored on YOUR OWN claude pid:** `basename(argv[0]) == node` AND the server entry point anywhere in the remaining argv; "ours" = the ancestor chain CONTAINS your own claude pid. **Record the foreign count BESIDE EVERY RESULT — including every server you boot OUTSIDE a hold.** **NEGATIVE controls, all in the same run, all must classify FOREIGN: the claude pids of the LIVE cockpit panes among `Datasec/NexusAI-M`, `-N`, `-O`, `-P`, `-R` and the coordinator pane `tuesday`, DERIVED LIVE by the launcher at launch and listed at the end of your prompt.** Re-read them at the start of every hold; **a hold with NO live negative control aborts.** Reuse gate 18's instrument BY COPY with YOUR pid as `ROOT` and these as `NEG` (`qa-floorlib18.sh`, defaults STALE) and `…/qa-floorcount.py`. Count every child you start and prove 0 left after each run (H-33).
4. **A zero is reportable only beside a control that fired in the same window** — the floor count, "nothing dials" (b2's base arm), "no write" (c2's base arm), "no pollution" (d2's base arm), "no forged line" (e2's base arm), "never gated" (g3's control), "LOST 0", "missing 0", "guarded by no cell" (the mutant LANDED and parsed).

**5. THE DEADLINE RULE — every probe, every child and every request has a per-step DEADLINE, a HEARTBEAT, and kills its child in a `finally`.**
Each step (offline npm ci 600 s, node driver 120 s, server boot 60 s, browser arm 180 s, lock arm 120 s, targeted jest 600 s, C-68 union 1,800 s, full verify 2,400 s, exit 25 s) has a written DEADLINE (`qa-to.sh`); a step past it is ABORTED and reported, never waited on. **Log a HEARTBEAT line at least every 2 minutes during any hold (H-4: a separate child, ≤ 120 s max gap, aborted if absent at 90 s); a step with no heartbeat for 5 minutes is aborted and reported,** and a hold that is not progressing releases the lock. Every process and child you start is killed in a `finally` (SIGTERM, then SIGKILL after a grace) **by pid from your own ancestry, never by pattern (C-174)**. **H-20 and H-21 apply to every jest.**

